From f15854bbcc7bc7980c2c6655ea709f47db0fff25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:52:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add physics_rate: step physics every Nth frame, or adaptively

Keeps every blob and every blob-to-blob bounce, but under load runs
chipmunk every 2nd/3rd frame with a correspondingly larger step, and
draws blobs extrapolated along their velocity in between so motion
stays smooth. Simulated time per drawn frame is unchanged.

- physics_rate: 1 (default) | 2 | 3 | auto
- auto adapts between 1 and 3 against a ~4 ms/frame physics budget
- --fast now means physics_rate: auto (instead of disabling
  collisions and capping blobs; those remain opt-in config options)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013kYwHzrj5ef427USqzf3UF
